  "notes": "Official cause code remains TBD/provisional per FORM-366; narrative identifies most-likely proximate cause as out-of-tolerance back plane connectors in the 22AC power cabinet control card cage, though testing of individual control cards found them fully functional, so root cause is not definitively established. AFW modeled as both an INVOLVES system (auto-actuated) and a mitigating response to the trip consequence, consistent with narrative describing it as an expected automatic response rather than a pre-event backup. No previous similar events reported in past three years, so no SIMILAR_TO stub LER was created. Bank C Group 2 control rods modeled as a Component (not System) since narrative treats them as physical rods sharing a common power/control cabinet."
